  "note": "Election of the whole council (21 members, seven for each ward) on 15 May 1939. Nominations on 5 May were followed by withdrawals in East and West, and on 13 May the local paper reported that there would be no contests in any ward (Mid-Ulster Mail, 13 May 1939, p. 6). William M'Guffin was the eighth nominee and withdrew. Returned unopposed."
